#
# Xorg packages that only Devuan gets, on top of packages/xorg.list.

# Devuan has no systemd-logind, so a session needs elogind to get one. Debian must not
# get these: systemd Conflicts elogind, and apt refuses the whole transaction.
#
#   E: Unable to satisfy dependencies. Reached two conflicting assignments:
#     - systemd:amd64=261.2-1 is not selected for install because:
#       1. elogind:amd64=255.17-1debian6 is selected for install
#       2. systemd:amd64=261.2-1 Conflicts elogind
#
# That made every Debian install with a graphical session impossible, and xorg is the
# default session. The old packages.csv had both lines in the shared xorg category, so
# this predates the split into per-distribution files.
libpam-elogind                  # login
elogind                         # login
